    "created_at": "2017-02-13T19:47:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-13T19:47:52Z",
    "body": "Am I correct that in terms of [ABNF specification](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5234#section-2.3) (RFC 5234) you can call \"@\" a unicode encoded terminal value?\r\n\r\n> **2.3.  Terminal Values**\r\n Rules resolve into a string of terminal values, sometimes called\r\n   characters.  In ABNF, a character is merely a non-negative integer.\r\n   In certain contexts, a specific mapping (encoding) of values into a\r\n   character set (such as ASCII) will be specified.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
